# Context

## Background
Task T009 (Looper backlog, milestone M2): translate SDL controller
and keyboard input into the core InputFrame of docs/SPEC.md section 5.

## Why This Way
The once-per-tick edge semantics live in the SDL-free InputAdapter
inside stackfall/input.hpp, so the portable suite (stackfall_tests)
can verify specification section 11 item 19 without linking SDL. The
SDL layer only maps events onto GameAction values; that keeps the
deterministic core free of platform types and keeps the mapping tables
in a single file (src/input_sdl.cpp) for the physical RG503 mapping
review.

## Gotchas
- SDL 2.30 auto-generates a default mapping for virtual joysticks of
  type SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_GAMECONTROLLER. The developer pad attaches as
  type UNKNOWN so a mapping test starts from an unmapped device and
  only SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG or addVirtualControllerMapping turns
  it into a controller.
- SDL_JoystickSetVirtualButton sets state; events appear on the next
  SDL_JoystickUpdate. A press and release inside one script pump
  produced no event at all until the script driver began calling
  SDL_JoystickUpdate after every pad command.
- Focus loss drops every source, not only the keyboard: releases for
  held pad buttons may never arrive after an overlay steals focus, and
  a re-press is safer than a stuck direction.

